title = {Sequencing of Modules and Prioritization of Test Cases using Dependency Structure Matrix: Survey},
abstract = {Software testing trying out is a proper manner in software program improvement life cycle, which is completed with the aid of committed testing team in which quantities of software program are examined with the intention of finding defects. Testing is not done, it concentrates on different test stages - Test Plan, Test Design, Test Execution, Defect Reporting & Tracking etc., writing of test cases based on specifications are the building blocks of testing that mainly occurs in test design stage. Test sequencing or prioritizing is a procedure of ordering the test cases in step with business needs to attain a positive aim. The main aim is to maximize the fault detection rate as early in the testing life cycle process. Test cases prioritization technique organizes test cases in sequencing order (either ascending or descending) such that test cases having high priority will be executed. This paper analysis the dependency structure algorithms so as to prioritize the test cases.},
