abstract = {The implementation of the submission of the State Civil Apparatus Wealth Report (LHKASN) is an obligation for all State Civil Apparatus (ASN) based on Ministry of State Apparatus Empowerment and Bureaucratic Reforms policy. Currently, the implementation of LHKASN in one of the state financial institutions still uses paper media as an LHKASN form. so that it can cause a human error in calculating assets. Besides, the LHKASN verification process is still carried out by typing the name of the ASN as an obligation to report one by one on the receipt which requires a lot of time so that the process is not efficient. Another problem is that no application can help monitor the discipline of ASN in delivering LHKASN, as well as data management related to the implementation of LHKASN which still uses the file system which is vulnerable to redundancies and data inconsistencies. Therefore, we need a system that can solve the existing problems. The method to be used in this research is the Incremental Model as a system development method with the Unified Modeling Language as a tool in designing the system. Meanwhile, for system testing, the method to be used is black-box testing by combining Boundary Value Analysis and Decision Table Testing. The result of this research is a web-based LHKASN application that can assist the reporting, verification, disciplinary monitoring, and data management processes in the implementation of LHKASN.},
