title = {Comparison of Current-Voltage Characteristics of Molybdenum Disulfide and Molybdenum Diselenide Channel Material Based Field Effect Transistor to optimize Conductance},
abstract = {The work aims to improve the current and conductance characteristics of molybdenum disulfide (MOS2) and compare it with molybdenum diselenide (MOSE2) in a Novel transistor by varying their oxide thickness ranging from 1 nm to 10 nm. The electrical conductance of MOS2 based 2D Field-effect transistor was compared with MOSE2 based novel transistor by varying the oxide thickness ranging from 1 nm to 10 nm in NanoHub© tool simulation environment. MOS2 based novel transistor has significantly higher conductance than MOSE2 based 2D FET. The optimal gate oxide thickness for maximum conductivity was 1 nm for MOSE2 based 2D FET and 10 nm for MOS2 based novel transistor. The results were obtained with a level of significance 0.01 and pretest power value of 80% using SPSS tools. Within the limit of study, MOS2 based novel 2D FET has better current (2899.72) and conductance (9.665e-03) mho characteristics than MOSE2 based 2D FET current (2882.55) and conductance (9.608e-03) mho.},
